# SQL Fundamentals Project – College Student Database Analysis

## 📌 Overview
This project demonstrates core SQL concepts through a structured **College Student Database**.  
It includes table creation, data insertion, updates, filtering, aggregation, grouping, and business logic such as grading and exam results.

The project is designed for **Business Analyst / Data Analyst** interview preparation and hands-on SQL practice.

---

## 🗂 Database Schema
**Table Name:** COLLEGE

| Column Name     | Data Type       |
|-----------------|-----------------|
| ID              | INT (Primary Key) |
| STUDENT_NAME    | VARCHAR(50) |
| CITY            | VARCHAR(50) |
| AGE             | INT |
| MARKS           | INT |
| GRADE           | VARCHAR(20) |
| EMAIL           | VARCHAR(100) |
| EXAM_RESULT     | VARCHAR(20) |

---

## ⚙ SQL Concepts Covered

### 1️⃣ Data Definition Language (DDL)
- CREATE TABLE
- ALTER TABLE (Add columns)

### 2️⃣ Data Manipulation Language (DML)
- INSERT
- UPDATE

### 3️⃣ Data Retrieval
- SELECT
- WHERE, BETWEEN, IN
- ORDER BY

### 4️⃣ Aggregations & Grouping
- COUNT, AVG, MAX
- GROUP BY
- HAVING

### 5️⃣ Conditional & Pattern Matching
- CASE WHEN
- LIKE
- DISTINCT
- NOT condition

---

## 📊 Business Logic Implemented
- Pass / Fail status based on marks
- Grade updates based on score range
- City-wise student analysis
- Email generation for students
- Ranking and filtering based on performance

---

## 🧪 Sample Queries Included
```sql
-- Students scoring 80 and above
SELECT STUDENT_NAME, CITY, MARKS
FROM COLLEGE
WHERE MARKS >= 80;

-- City-wise average marks
SELECT CITY, AVG(MARKS)
FROM COLLEGE
GROUP BY CITY
ORDER BY AVG(MARKS) DESC;

-- Pass / Fail classification
UPDATE COLLEGE
SET EXAM_RESULT =
CASE
  WHEN MARKS > 60 THEN 'PASS'
  ELSE 'FAIL'
END;

🚀 Use Case
SQL interview preparation
Beginner-to-intermediate SQL practice
Business Analyst / Data Analyst portfolio project

🛠 Tools Used
PostgreSQL / MySQL (SQL standard syntax)
